  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nSynoptic high pressure continues building in Tuesday, and a surface \nlow to the west helps to advect warmer air into our western \ncounties, resulting in highs in the upper-90s here with temps \ntopping out closer to 90 elsewhere. Wednesday will be a couple of \ndegrees warmer still ahead of troughing pushing rain through SOMO \nWednesday night into late week. The axis of the trough, which will \nbring the first round of rain, appears to be followed by one or more \nshortwaves that will continue to bring rain chances for a couple of \ndays. Long term guidance indicates PoPs ranging from around 30% \nalong the Springfield latitude to around 60 percent into our \nnorthern counties beginning Wednesday night. Odds are currently \nslightly lower Thursday night through Friday, topping out around 30-\n40%. The SPC has mentioned the potential for inclusion of portions \nof the area in future severe weather outlooks, but certainty and \ncoverage are too low at this time.\n\nThe initial front appears to stall out as it brings this activity to \nour area and eventually retreats to the north, leaving us without a \ntrue frontal passage. We will keep our steadily warming airmass \naround, and it may have the potential to warm into Extreme territory \nby next weekend into mid-August.",
